Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 22:14:11 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(linux): build saints reborn's sdk patch outside windows

Saints Reborn's patches/rexglue-sdk.patch calls a few Win32 functions
outside its _WIN32 blocks, so the runtime and the GPU plugin do not
build on Linux:

- rex/win32_shims.h gives Linux and macOS GetTickCount64, Sleep,
  GetCurrentProcessId and SOCKET, and REX_SR_EXPORT for the functions
  the game looks up by name (__declspec(dllexport) on Windows, default
  visibility elsewhere).
- select: the wait that also wakes on other UDP sockets passes the
  highest descriptor + 1 (Windows ignores it) and stops at FD_SETSIZE
  without Windows' fd_count; getsockname and getsockopt take a
  socklen_t.
- online_identity: the executable folder, the random install id and
  the machine and user names come from POSIX; the owner key (reserved
  names) stays Windows-only, so elsewhere reserved names stay reserved.
- xsocket includes netdb.h for getaddrinfo; xgi_live names its
  dependent TranslateVirtual template, which MSVC does not require.
---
